  "answer": "The goal was not met: only one of the five cases was confirmed. It is S1, on scene 023b7fcc, with the lead car shifted 1.5 s earlier and slowed to 0.5x, and every run there rear-ended it. Blame for those crashes is unclear. Each time, the replay had already put the ego very close behind a slower lead car before the policy took over, and the ego was still on the recorded path. So this case may show how the setup was built more than a policy weakness. Most of the other failures were not rear-ends. On scene 12855a41 the ego steered into a car in the next lane or drove off the road, and on 19f339ba the ego was hit from behind after braking with nothing ahead. The one other rear-end, on 19f339ba at -0.5 s and 0.75x, comes from a single run, so it is a hint and not a rate.",
